<Base title="Pikobuy Returns and Exchanges | Eligibility, Timing & Evidence" description="Check Pikobuy's warehouse return window, seller eligibility, evidence to include and fees to confirm before submitting a request.">
  <PageHead title="Pikobuy returns and exchanges" copy="Review the seller’s return terms when choosing a listing, then act on any issue as soon as your warehouse photos arrive."/>
  <section class="container section reading">
    <article>
      <h2>Check eligibility before ordering</h2>
      <p>Pikobuy’s policy ties the standard warehouse return process to seller eligibility, the condition required for resale and the time since warehouse entry. Check the seller’s terms for your specific product. Common exclusions listed by Pikobuy include customized orders, second-hand items and certain items whose seals, tags or packaging have been removed.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.pikobuy.com/protocol/returns" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Check the official returns and exchanges policy</a></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Use the warehouse status to check timing</h2>
      <p>Pikobuy’s application instructions give a standard window of 120 hours for eligible items, counted from the hour after the order status changes to <strong>In Warehouse</strong>. Check the order page and submit promptly if you need a return. For an exchange, ask support to confirm the seller’s options and the applicable deadline.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Show what differs from the order</h2>
      <p>Open the Pikobuy order and use its after-sales option when available. Choose the reason that matches what happened. Include the order reference, exact variant ordered, photo of the received label or issue, and the resolution you want. Keep the item out of the international parcel while the request is open.</p>
      <p>For a wrong size, for example, give the selected size and attach a clear photo of the received size tag. If a seam is damaged, include one close-up and one wider photo that shows where the damage is.</p>
      <p><a class="text-link" href="/qc/#qc-checklist">Review the QC checklist</a></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Keep evidence while the request is open</h2>
      <p>Save the order details, the timestamp for warehouse entry, the original seller options and photos of the issue. Keep the packaging and tags required for resale where possible. If a part is missing, list what you bought and ask the warehouse for a single photo showing everything that arrived.</p>
      <p>Record the request reference and any quoted return costs. Seller acceptance and the reason for the request can affect which charges apply. Keep the item at the warehouse while checking the outcome.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Confirm who pays and what the seller accepts</h2>
      <p>Costs can depend on the reason, whether the seller accepts the return and the delivery charges involved. A buyer-requested return can include return postage, original delivery charges and a handling fee. If the seller sent the wrong item or the item arrived damaged, give Pikobuy the evidence and ask who will cover the charges in your case.</p>
      <p>If you purchased the item independently and used Pikobuy only to forward it, contact the original seller or sender for after-sales support. Pikobuy’s forwarding terms say it can help send the goods back. <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pikobuy.com/protocol/shipping" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Official forwarding terms</a>.</p>
    </article>
    <p class="notice">Check the seller’s response and charges shown for your actual request. <a class="text-link" href="https://www.pikobuy.com/contact" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Contact Pikobuy support</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
